                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c53b328-89b7-4129-8d44-a3274267c160",
                        "source_entry_id": "288dc0f1-0e41-313c-97cf-388702e80448",
                        "source_sense_id": "fcba1a1c-018d-3d5d-828b-672a93c8395a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Celle qui tient un restaurant",
                        "target_lang_word": "restaurateuse",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "restaurateuse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                        "entry_id": "0e1f011d-03f7-308e-8936-8f13d9bd12f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female restaurateur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dfbf91b-8bf9-4bfb-96ba-e60bdbb17c11",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "Jonathan Hazard remembered, ‘Lee takes being a restaurateuse very seriously. Do you know she won’t marry me because she might have to give it up if she did?’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e050a4ba-ad0c-4995-93f4-2a21a12ebddf",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "We were sitting in a studio, an odd mix of people who included another now good friend, Myrtle Allen of Ballymaloe House in Ireland. She is a restaurateuse of great distinction, suitably garlanded by Michelin, and she had just opened an eating house in Paris."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fee3623-2ab0-49c0-be83-39135f79b1c7",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "“When I was a little teenager, I was workin’” – restaurateuse. Rancher: “Kids don’t realize.” “My kids say, ‘Don’t talk about the dark ages.’ I say to them, ‘You may be seein’ more of ’em!’” Talking, refills author’s coffee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0b53b95-a7d6-42e7-99b2-0e067f9cea8c",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "It's not a spin-off, since none of the characters are the same. (the fact that the actress is the same doesn't make it a spin-off--in Cheers she played a cheery British barmaid and in C.A. she was a crusty American restaurateuse.) However, it is an example of a rip-off sitcom (using the same basic premise that has succeeded elsewhere)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bbd2f37-3d6d-4dd0-8ab0-ba8d62d5c1b6",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "It was on that occasion and many more like it that I got to know a great Morelian cook and restaurateuse, Livier Ruiz, who has become a cherished friend. I have published a few of her recipes before and here is one of hers and two simple ones from the food fair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bfb4288-f3c1-47e3-ab1f-24bc0656b7cc",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "<> / Uh, make that Costa Rica. I've had a problem with vowels ever since I read the following in the NY Post: / >RESTAURATEUSE Hayne Jason - who / >describes her Lucky Cheng's as an Epcot / >center for fetishists - hopes Ivana Trump / >has a thick skin. The 4,000 color / >brochures which just came back from the / >printer contain several photos of celebrity / >patrons. But the caption under one / >identifies The Donald's first wife as Ivana / >Tramp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e365a50e-e69b-4c4e-8b23-6c218a0036cc",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "I enjoyed the review of Empress of India; Scott was the one that turned us on to it. Jeannie is one of the few restaurateuses that is willing to work with my wife's celiac disease; she regards it as a challenge to her artistry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e84c568e-d48a-4fab-bb3b-4589ec994e65",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "The Grauniad had an interview last month with no. 66, a San Francisco restaurateur (or rather restaurateuse) with Norwegian and Brazilian citizenship."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33d3b244-aaeb-4377-9ccc-13d717fe616c",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "A hot dog stand with an adjoining picnic table would qualify as a \"restaurant.\" In the spectrum of dining establishments, a Subway or other fast-food franchise is more of a food factory than a service establishment. The savvy needed to operate one is different from, say, managing La Mer Duquesne, a Dennys, or even a chain of IHOPs. To own/operate a franchise may very well be demanding and entrepreneurial, but to call her a restaurateur (restaurateuse?) is stretching the connotation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6979e05e-f33a-43fb-9a44-6e87f74a9032",
                                                "sense_id": "6a027a63-7aaa-3099-b9d6-336c11fff637",
                                                "text": "As all hostesses should, Cassie and Kim were putting serious thought into the party planning. At bedtime, with Kim already tucked up and Cassie lingering on the outskirts of her sister’s room in her nightie and a pair of her mother’s old walking socks, they were bandying menus like a pair of rival restaurateuses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bba9e90a-826a-4a1e-9c69-d19062b06e2f",
                        "source_entry_id": "288dc0f1-0e41-313c-97cf-388702e80448",
                        "source_sense_id": "fcba1a1c-018d-3d5d-828b-672a93c8395a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Celle qui tient un restaurant",
                        "target_lang_word": "restauratrice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "restauratrice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                        "entry_id": "2315fc16-41c7-36d4-99ce-e17e309e2fe7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female restaurateur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41e5ee35-51fa-4796-b9ec-601934e2482a",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "Gerda Simonson, a Swedish restauratrice with many years of experience in New York, has compiled three hundred choice recipes for snacks and tidbits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f905e7f1-929e-4e60-916e-e5926eebeccd",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "A restauratrice seated on a Socony can. She has a tray with bananas, bread and a tin pot of bean-paste soup."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "228b1eb1-a375-43c4-a1b1-9dec95a54d6a",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "Away from his occupational Hell, nothing is happier than Kyffin dancing a gangling Welsh reel, or being proposed to by a vast Alsatian restauratrice in Soho."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb58a8f9-2b42-4366-b514-588c15583d12",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "A restauratrice who fired the dishwasher and let her dog clean the plates by licking them should be given a five-month suspended sentence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69b01146-85cd-4cc6-ac78-f095b2fcd105",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "Well, there you have a glimpse of Eleanor Patricia Murphy Kiernan, restauratrice and business woman, horticulturist, horsewoman, aviatrix, hostess and world traveller as the world sees her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02f94cd6-3b96-462e-b25f-4db6b101aa14",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "The appellant, Helen Chavez, is a restauratrice in Tampa[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fef0e359-9653-4c45-acac-6e87e72e5d00",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "Rosalie, for example, the restauratrice in the Rue Campagne-Première, in whose hole-in-the-wall everyone ate—Modigliani, Jeanne Hébuterne, Vlaminck, even, it is said, Picasso—called him Amedeo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "407e3976-9c6b-47f2-90d8-a51a0dd38c58",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "As if the Nygren/Dailey saga didn’t already sound too eventful to be true, Steve Nygren added the final romantic touch by choosing as his bride the daughter of one of Atlanta’s most famous regional restauratrices, Margaret Kennon Lupo, of Mary Mac’s."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e4fb1b3-944b-4f44-a5f5-6bdec5cb7f86",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "Sturdily English working-class, she was free of those strange bonds, of continental provenance, in part traditionally filial, in part traditionally economic, that fettered Adelaide to her mother, Madame Foltinowicz, as her literary descendant Annette was fettered to that other redoubtable Soho restauratrice, Madame Lamotte."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e31731e-368b-4ea2-809b-4dd0d5accd6b",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "A similar outfit had been commissioned by Gloria Magnus, the Capri-based Cockney socialite and restauratrice whom Maria had met during one her trips to see Gracie Fields – a notorious man-eater whom one journalist had described as ‘coming free with every course’, and at least one Italian newspaper drew comparisons between the two."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b312c9b-3310-409a-9188-9870df6f8521",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "My proudest moment as a seasoned restauratrice took place one afternoon at Chez Panisse several years ago, when Richard rose to speak to a group of French winemakers he was accompanying on a tour of California wineries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c190d2e-6677-4ae2-9156-5f80a24d4e30",
                                                "sense_id": "69dbad53-0c09-3961-b535-7daacff2e0f0",
                                                "text": "Though in fact I’m on my way to a harvest lunch hosted by legendary restauratrice Alice Waters in honor of Cannard, who for 21 years has supplied the majority of produce for Chez Panisse, in spirit I find myself within scrabbling distance of my childhood, and suddenly I am sobbing so hard I have to pull over."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
